WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.340
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, since so many
of you asked me to say something about the

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:13.840
Spider-Man Marvel Sony stuff I thought I’d
do something fun and list my Top 5 new actors

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.730
I think could pull off peter parker.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:20.440
There are so many reasons why Spiderman might
never appear in a Marvel film so I’ll do

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.240
a breakdown of the bigger ones.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.410
Don’t get super excited.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.089
Most of you will probably have one or more
children before Peter Parker ever gets invited

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:30.190
to a party in the Avengers Tower.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.230
Important stuff first everyone has already
been spamming new actors for Spider-Man.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:39.999
In case you don’t know, Marvel wants to
show Andrew Garfield the door.

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:42.829
I guess they’re not huge fans of his.

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:46.269
That doesn’t mean they hate him, it just
means if they used Spiderman, they wanted

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:48.420
a fresh take on the character.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.510
If Andrew Garfield guest starred in Civil
War or Infinity War he’d bring all the Amazing

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.799
Spider-Man movie baggage with him.

00:00:55.799 --> 00:00:58.879
Marvel wants absolutely nothing to do with
any pre-existing Spider-Man movies.

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:00.280
Even the Sam Raimi ones.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.920
Normally this wouldn’t be a huge deal, but
Sony Re-Booted Spider-Man with Garfield incredibly

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:04.970
fast after Spider-Man 3.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.350
And he’s currently under contract for 2
more sequels, that includes Spider-Man 4.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.250
When they announced all those Spider-Man Spinoff
movies, he wasn’t a part of that.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.490
Spider-Man wasn’t going to be a big character
in those.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.960
Cut to the giant mess of developmental hell.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:24.549
A lot of big producers signed to work on those
films had to bail because it was taking too

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:26.829
long to get Sinister Six, Venom and the other
movies going.

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:29.909
Which is when the Marvel Spider-Man talk started
happening.

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.829
As much as Sony’s film unit has been in
decline, Marvel has been on a home run streak.

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:37.909
The only reason they haven’t reached a deal
yet is because of money.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:41.939
Marvel wants a lot and sony doesn’t want
to give them the majority of the profits from

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:42.939
any crossovers.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:43.939
So will it ever happen, probably.

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:45.020
Will it happen in the next 10 years?

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.020
Maybe.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.020
And only with a new actor.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.899
Thus, here are my TOP 5 candidates for a new
Peter Parker.

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:54.289
I’m going to do a thumbs up thumbs down
for each of these and I’ll address the Miles

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:55.289
Morales comments after.

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:57.259
Number 5 - Dylan O’Brien

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:00.979
Thumbs Up: He has genre experience and most
of the characters he’s played have been

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:02.350
Peter Parker types.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.579
So he knows the drill.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:07.619
And no matter which Marvel film Spider-Man
appears in, it’s only going to be a supporting

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:08.619
role.

00:02:08.619 --> 00:02:11.180
So he won’t be completely responsible for
carrying the story.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:16.390
He’s got name level recognition even though
I consider him a B-Level blockbuster star.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.660
Marvel tends to go after actors that are on
the rise so they don’t have to pay their

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.660
actors too much.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:21.660
Robert Downey Jr is the exception.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.030
They cast him before they started their 6-picture
deal standard contract.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.850
Thumbs down on Dylan: Even though Spider-Man
would only be a supporting character, a bad

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.430
choice of actor could sink the movie.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:34.890
Spider-Man is a huge deal.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:42.960
No matter how much we see him on screen.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.020
Number 4 - Ansel Elgort

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.800
Thumbs Up: He’s a great with Drama, and
Spider-Man drama is at the core of the Civil

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.420
War comic book storyline.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.960
Marvel isn’t doing the comic book storyline
for Civil War, but they can graft some of

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.400
that into Avengers Infinity War.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.230
Anytime he’s with the Avengers, Spider-Man
is a boy being taken advantage of by Asshole

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.650
older Heroes.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:09.860
He’s like the impressionable little brother.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.330
So if they want to stay true to that, Elgort
can play that.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.330
And he’s the right age.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.720
A very young 20 something Spiderman.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.680
He even looks like he could still be in high
school if they want to go that young.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.680
Thumbs Down:

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:26.280
They only real experience he has in an action
movie is the Divergent Trilogy.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:32.570
And he hasn’t shown that he can pull off
that twitchy hyper active quality that Peter

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:33.870
Parker has.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:37.230
Number 3 - Anton Yelchin

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:42.560
Thumbs Up: He has a strong indie drama experience
and big blockbuster genre experience.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.370
Chekov kind of is the Peter Parker of the
Enterprise in the new JJ Abrams films.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:51.400
Plus he’s even wearing Spider-Man red now.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.710
Thumbs Down: scheduling conflicts with the
Star Trek Sequels could be a problem.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.600
They haven’t set a date for Star Trek 3
yet, but it’s happening.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.470
After that there’s potential for them writing
in a new cast.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:06.270
Or writing out Chekov so he’d be free to
do other really big movies.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:11.890
Typically big movies can shoot for up to 6
months, not including re-shoots and the time

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.000
they have to spend promoting the film all
over the world.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.720
So scheduling is the big reason this probably
won’t happen.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.690
Number 2 - Nicholas Hoult

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.900
Thumbs Up: All the same reasons as Anton Yelchin.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:25.810
But I feel like Nicholas Hoult has a little
more on screen presence and he can carry a

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:29.030
big movie.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.030
Thumbs Down:

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.330
Same reason as Chekov.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.650
The X-Men Franchise is in the middle of making
Apocalypse, they’ll be shooting soon.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:40.490
Small upside, the cast of those movies are
so big that they can easily write Beast out

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:50.650
of the films without a lot 
of explanation.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:56.790
Number 1 - Jamie Dornan

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:00.680
Thumbs Up: He’s getting ready to be the
biggest star on the planet once Fifty Shades

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.880
of Grey comes out next year.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:08.520
He can carry a film, he’s not super expensive
because he’s still considered an up and

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.520
comer.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:15.280
And he has a lot of genre experience.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.280
Thumbs Down:

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:21.000
He’s probably too old to play Peter Parker.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.790
No way can he pull off impressionable youth
living with Thor, Iron Man and Captain America

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:38.030
next door.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:41.400
If they decide to go with an older spider
man, then it might work.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.470
And he’s currently not signed to another
mega-franchise yet.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:52.510
Although they probably will do a Fifty Shades
sequel.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:06:00.820
So what about the Miles Morales Spider Man?

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:07.240
The reason people aren’t talking about him
with marvel a lot is because Avi Arad and

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:21.290
Matt Tolmach, the producers of Spider-Man
have said the character will only ever be

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.290
Peter Parker.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:30.100
Legally right now, they control that kind
of thing, no matter if Sony gives the character

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.100
to Marvel.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:34.830
So if you want Miles Morales, you have to
get the rights away from them.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:35.830
Not Sony.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.340
I know it sounds confusing.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:47.150
But they have the rights to the character
and they signed a long term contract with

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.150
Sony.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:54.710
Next Big Question: Say it all works out and
Sony Agrees to share Spider-Man with Marvel

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:55.940
before they shoot Civil War.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:57.581
What does Marvel do with the character?

00:06:57.581 --> 00:07:01.930
Easy answer, he gets introduced in a supporting
role in Civil War and then becomes a fullblown

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:05.020
Avenger sometime during the first Infinity
War.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.280
Like a battlefield promotion.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:10.120
The Thumbs down on this is that they probably
won’t reach a deal in time to get him into

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.780
Civil War, at least for a meaningful role.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:18.960
They’ve already written the script for the
movie, it’s not going to be based on the

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.000
Comic Book Civil War.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.790
I know this pisses some of you off, but they’ve
already changed so much of the comics.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.480
The biggest thing being Ultron and The Vision’s
backstories.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.000
So Civil War will not revolve around Identity.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Second Thumbs Down:

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.130
If he becomes part of the Marvel movies, Sony
won’t be able to make Spider-Man movies

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.130
the way they want.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:40.280
Marvel would have to be given control of the
character, and starting in 2017 Marvel has

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.280
three movies scheduled.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.560
Guardians 2, Thor 3 and Black Panther.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.350
When you also consider the DC and Star Wars
films coming out that year, it looks way too

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:49.990
crowded to support a solo Spider-Man film.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:56.380
Meaning Sony would lose the lion’s share
of it’s biggest box office franchise.

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.860
And Sony as a company has been doing terribly
lately.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:04.500
There’s no way they can go 6 or 7 years
without the money from a solo spider-man film.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:09.919
James Bond, their next biggest franchise,
isn’t enough to carry the studio by itself.

00:08:09.919 --> 00:08:15.960
Those I think are the biggest reasons why
this Spider-Man marvel thing won’t work

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.000
out the way we want it to.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.949
I think it’s more likely that it would happen
after Avengers Infinity War.

00:08:22.949 --> 00:08:34.099
By that time, they can re-cast a lot of the
bigger marvel actors like Captain America,

00:08:34.099 --> 00:08:43.430
Thor, so the marvel verse will be changing
enough to accommodate Spider-man in a big

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:53.100
way with a new actor.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:09:01.009
It also gives Sony the time to get it’s
shit together to the point where it’s financially

00:09:01.009 --> 00:09:02.949
feasible for it to sign a bunch of profits
away in lost Spider-Man solo films.

00:09:02.949 --> 00:09:03.949
Here’s the long shot.

00:09:03.949 --> 00:09:06.449
They’re still casting Civil War, they won’t
start shooting till late spring next year.

00:09:06.449 --> 00:09:07.610
After the Avengers 2 press tour.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:10.850
So if we don’t hear anything official about
a new actor being cast as Spider-Man before

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:11.850
Avengers 2 comes out.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:12.850
Don’t plan on it happening.

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:18.470
Here’s my big question for you guys would
you rather see Spider-Man as a small background

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.410
character in Avengers Infinity War.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:32.980
Or would you be willing to wait till Phase
4 for 

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:48.540
him if he could be a major character in the
marvel universe.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.529
So is it cameo right now or big freaking deal
in 5 years.

00:09:51.529 --> 00:09:58.130
I would rather wait and see them doing something
more canonical but I’m not going to flip

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:18.480
if he gets a small cameo that has absolutely
nothing to do with the comics.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:24.040
Right now it’s a fascinating idea, it just
doesn’t seem like a reality.

